# DDR4 overlay for GXL boards whose product defconfig does not set DRAM_*.
# Apply after spl-usb.config (which hard-codes CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=912 for the
# DDR3 Le Potato profile).
#
# NOTHING BUILDS THIS FRAGMENT (measured 2026-08-30). No config in
# libretech-builder-simple names spl-usb-ddr4 at all, and the target this
# header used to claim -- aml-s905x-cc-v2-libre -- builds the CHAIN instead:
#   UBOOT_TARGET="libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig tpl-spl-chain.config \
#                 olddefconfig"
# and its own header says "do NOT add spl-usb.config". The single-stage
# USB+DDR4 composition this fragment completes was superseded at 584916c96db
# (one defconfig per board); the only other in-tree reference to it is
# libretech-cc_v2_libre_defconfig:4, which already calls it "Formerly stacked".
#
# The recipe below is unbuilt, not broken -- it still links, and narrowly:
#   make libretech-cc_v2_defconfig spl-usb.config spl-usb-ddr4.config \
#        olddefconfig
# passes at 40851 B with 109 B of guaranteed-usable headroom, the narrowest
# OK in the GX build matrix. Anything that wires this up is a size tripwire.
#
# Numbers match vendor boot-lite aml-s905x-cc-v2 + libretech-cc_v2_spl_defconfig:
#   DDR4, 1080 MHz, 1 rank, 1024 MB, 2T.
#
# Size: DRAM_DDR4 + stepped training overflows the 0xb000 SRAM budget by ~2 KiB
# on top of the DDR3 USB profile (measured 2026-08-09: +2072 B). Drop SPL MMC
# for this USB-only profile — pass-1/pass-2 never touch MMC; product U-Boot
# still has full MMC. That recovers the headroom for the DDR4 train path.
# CONFIG_DRAM_DDR3 is not set
CONFIG_DRAM_DDR4=y
CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=1080
CONFIG_DRAM_ONE_RANK=y
CONFIG_DRAM_2T_MODE=y
CONFIG_DRAM_DQS_CORR=y
# CONFIG_SPL_MMC is not set
# CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY is not set
# CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_USE_SECTOR is not set
